{
    "Read Me": [
        {
            "Description: Information in this spreadsheet represents metadata described in the QRS Supplement to the SDTMIG. This spreadsheet is generated from CDISC Controlled Terminology in CDISC Library. One spreadsheet is available per QRS instrument, per version (as designated in QRS Supplement to the SDTMIG). The layout of the spreadsheet provides a combined, simplified view of CDISC Controlled Terminology and information in the \"All Published QRS Supplements\" section of the CDISC QRS standards page. The purpose of the spreadsheet is to aid implementers in creating SDTMIG-based datasets.": "About the use of Code: Code (i.e., unique numeric code assigned by NCI EVS, in C<<number>> format) is used so that information presented is agnostic to different versions of CDISC Controlled Terminology publications, where Code is immutable in principal and other information such as Submission Value may vary. Users will have the flexibility to pair the Code information with any given publication of their choice.",
            "Unnamed: 1": NaN
        },
        {
            "Description: Information in this spreadsheet represents metadata described in the QRS Supplement to the SDTMIG. This spreadsheet is generated from CDISC Controlled Terminology in CDISC Library. One spreadsheet is available per QRS instrument, per version (as designated in QRS Supplement to the SDTMIG). The layout of the spreadsheet provides a combined, simplified view of CDISC Controlled Terminology and information in the \"All Published QRS Supplements\" section of the CDISC QRS standards page. The purpose of the spreadsheet is to aid implementers in creating SDTMIG-based datasets.": "Statement on copyright permission: A QRS Supplement to the SDTMIG may be for an instrument in the a public domain or for a copyrighted instrument for which the copyright holder has given CDISC permission to develop a supplement. All QRS Supplements to the SDTMIG are created in compliance with CDISC operating procedure COP-001. For copyrighted instruments, note the following:",
            "Unnamed: 1": NaN
        },
        {
            "Description: Information in this spreadsheet represents metadata described in the QRS Supplement to the SDTMIG. This spreadsheet is generated from CDISC Controlled Terminology in CDISC Library. One spreadsheet is available per QRS instrument, per version (as designated in QRS Supplement to the SDTMIG). The layout of the spreadsheet provides a combined, simplified view of CDISC Controlled Terminology and information in the \"All Published QRS Supplements\" section of the CDISC QRS standards page. The purpose of the spreadsheet is to aid implementers in creating SDTMIG-based datasets.": "Granting CDISC the right to create supplements to represent an instrument in CDISC QRS domains is not a license for CDISC standards users to use the instrument without complying with the copyright holders licensing requirements.\n\nNo part of a copyrighted instrument or accompanying guidelines may be reproduced, distributed, or transmitted in any form, or by any means, including photocopying, recording, or other electronic or mechanical methods without the permission of the copyright holder and payment of applicable fees.",
            "Unnamed: 1": NaN
        },
